# Astona site: environment template.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# NEVER COMMIT .env (it is in .gitignore). If a real .env was ever committed, treat every value in it as
# leaked: rotate it. Values below are placeholders. Do not put `$` or spaces in values (compose env_file
# does not interpolate; keep them plain). Used by docker-compose.prod.yml via `env_file: .env`.
#
# Legend:  [REQUIRED-PROD] must be set in production | [OPTIONAL] | [DEV-ONLY] never set in production

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [REQUIRED-PROD] Application DB user. Generate passwords with: openssl rand -base64 24 | tr -d '/+=\n'
WORDPRESS_DB_NAME=astona
WORDPRESS_DB_USER=astona
WORDPRESS_DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_db_password
# [REQUIRED-PROD] MariaDB root password (db container init and scripts/backup.sh). Note: the wordpress/cron
# containers also receive it through env_file; keep the host and compose project private.
MARIADB_ROOT_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_db_root_password

# --- Plugin: coaching-platform (read with getenv() or a wp-config constant of the same name) ----------
# [REQUIRED-PROD] Encrypts applicant ID numbers and queued SMS payloads (libsodium secretbox).
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32      (base64 of 32 random bytes)
# LOSING THIS KEY MAKES STORED ID NUMBERS UNRECOVERABLE and it is NOT included in backups. Store a copy in
# a password manager / secret manager, separate from the backup storage. Outside WP_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE=local
# the site refuses to run without it.
CC_ENC_KEY=CHANGE_ME_base64_of_32_random_bytes

# [REQUIRED-PROD] Directory for applicant photos, outside the web root. Compose sets it to the
# private_data volume mount, /var/www/private (set in docker-compose.prod.yml; listed here for reference).
# CC_PRIVATE_DIR=/var/www/private

# [REQUIRED-PROD] Payment driver: `bkash` (the `fake` driver is REFUSED outside local/development).
# Payments return 503 while unset.
# CC_PAYMENT_GATEWAY=bkash
# [REQUIRED-PROD when CC_PAYMENT_GATEWAY=bkash] bKash Tokenized Checkout merchant credentials.
# BKASH_MODE must be exactly `sandbox` or `live`. Register https://<site>/wp-json/cc/v1/payments/callback with bKash.
# BKASH_MODE=sandbox
# BKASH_APP_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# BKASH_APP_SECRET=CHANGE_ME
# BKASH_USERNAME=CHANGE_ME
# BKASH_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME

# [REQUIRED-PROD] Primary SMS driver (credentials and OTP SMS fail without it). `fake` is dev-only.
# [OPTIONAL] CC_SMS_FALLBACK is tried after the primary fails 3 times.
# Drivers: bulksmsbd, greenweb (fake is dev-only). Credentials for the drivers you use:
# BULKSMSBD_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# BULKSMSBD_SENDER_ID=CHANGE_ME
# GREENWEB_TOKEN=CHANGE_ME
# CC_SMS_PRIMARY=bulksmsbd
# CC_SMS_FALLBACK=greenweb

# --- Google Analytics 4 (optional) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measurement ID turns on the consent banner and browser events; the API secret additionally enables the
# server-side payment_success event (Measurement Protocol). Both unset = no analytics at all.
# GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX
# GA4_API_SECRET=CHANGE_ME

# [DEV-ONLY] CC_RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED=1 disables rate limits and is ignored unless WP_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE=local.
# Intentionally NOT listed as a setting here. Do not add it to a production .env.

# --- Cloudflare Turnstile (contact form captcha) ------------------------------------------------------
# [REQUIRED-PROD] Contact submissions are refused outside local/development when the secret is missing.
# Also readable as wp-config constants TURNSTILE_SECRET / TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY.
TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=CHANGE_ME_turnstile_site_key
TURNSTILE_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_turnstile_secret

# --- Compose runtime ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [OPTIONAL] Host port on 127.0.0.1 that the TLS reverse proxy forwards to (default 8080).
# WEB_PORT=8080

# --- scripts/backup.sh and scripts/restore.sh (read from the environment of the operator/cron) --------
# Backups contain PII (names, phone numbers, encrypted ID numbers, applicant photos). Encrypt them and
# restrict access. These are NOT read by the website.
#
# Encryption (one of; backup.sh refuses to run with neither unless BACKUP_ALLOW_UNENCRYPTED=1):
#   age (preferred, authenticated):  AGE_RECIPIENT=age1...     restore: AGE_IDENTITY_FILE=/path/key.txt
#   openssl AES-256-CBC+PBKDF2:      BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=...     (openssl rand -base64 32)
# BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/astona
# AGE_RECIPIENT=
# AGE_IDENTITY_FILE=
# BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=
# RETENTION_DAILY=30
# RETENTION_MONTHLY=12
#
# Optional off-host push with restic (S3/R2). restic encrypts its repository with RESTIC_PASSWORD.
# RESTIC_REPOSITORY=s3:https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/<bucket>/astona
# RESTIC_PASSWORD=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
